       ttuunnee22ffss allows the system administrator to adjust various tunable  file
       system  parameters on Linux ext2, ext3, or ext4 file systems.  The cur‐
       rent values of these options can be displayed by using the --ll option to
       ttuunnee22ffss(8) program, or by using the dduummppee22ffss(8) program.

       The  _d_e_v_i_c_e  specifier can either be a filename (i.e., /dev/sda1), or a
       LABEL or UUID specifier: "LLAABBEELL==_v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l" or  "UUUUIIDD==_u_u_i_d".   (i.e.,
       LABEL=home or UUID=e40486c6-84d5-4f2f-b99c-032281799c9d).

